# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# This site loads nothing from anywhere. There is no CDN, no analytics, no
# remote font and no network call at runtime, so the policy below is the
# enforceable form of that claim rather than a description of it.
#
# style-src has no 'unsafe-inline': the page carries no style attributes and no
# inline <style> block, and the stagger delays and stack-logo colours that once
# used them are ordinary classes. Setting element.style from script is CSSOM
# rather than an inline style, so the reading-progress bar is unaffected.
#
# connect-src is 'self' rather than 'none' because wasm-bindgen's web target
# loads the module with fetch(), which connect-src governs; under 'none' the
# audit module simply cannot instantiate. 'self' still means this page can only
# ever talk to its own origin, and there is no origin API to talk to, so the
# claim "nothing leaves this page" is unchanged. The alternative that would keep
# 'none' is embedding the module as base64 in a script, which costs a third more
# bytes to buy a distinction without a difference here.
#
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is the ONE token WebAssembly instantiation requires, and it
# is exactly that: permission to compile a wasm module, not permission to eval
# JavaScript. It does not weaken connect-src, so the audit module still cannot
# reach the network. The alternative, 'unsafe-eval', would be strictly worse and
# is not needed.
#
# Cache-control: index.html, the stylesheet and the script are revalidated every
# time, because this site has no content-hashed filenames and a stale app.js
# against a fresh index.html would silently break the figures. The fonts and the
# paper PDF are immutable in practice and are cached for a week.
#
# `/` needs its own rule, and it is the ONLY rule that matters for the page.
# Pages answers `/index.html` with a 308 redirect to `/`, so a `/index.html`
# entry decorates a redirect and never reaches the document; without the `/`
# entry the page fell through to the `/*` default and served a stale copy for
# several minutes after a deploy. The `/index.html` line below is kept only so
# that a direct request for it is not cached either. Measured, not theorised.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/pkg/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, immutable
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/mechanism_interferometry.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
